      <activity id="c09f9300-b8af-53b5-927b-4fe678a1829a" activityNameId="7555913a-3aaa-5b74-815b-a9e372cb4538" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Gold, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Gold, at refinery
This data set describes the beneficiation, concentration and refinement of gold.;
CAS number: 007440-57-5; 
UUID: 8f784b52-8ff6-3128-a7a9-363314b8d605
This data set describes the mining of gold concentrate in United States. It includes energy and water consumption, land use, transports, waste disposal as well as emissions to air and water.
Location: Material requirements for gold concentration are estimated with Australian data, emissions to water and air are estimated with Australian data
Technology: The mining of ore from open pit and underground mines is considered.
Time period: Period of public environmental report
Production volume: 183.34 t gold
Sampling: environmental report 
Extrapolations: See Geography, several values have been scaled from one mine
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8f784b52-8ff6-3128-a7a9-363314b8d605.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="9aaa4753-f7ef-5e0d-bcb0-bc5f01164c5b" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
